@startuml persistence-model
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
title What a crash keeps: the persistence model behind gaze-fs, MemFs and ProfileStartup.tla

component "F1R3Gaze\n(writes through gaze-fs)" as App #DDEBF7

rectangle "Kernel: what every process sees" as Kernel #E2EFDA {
  component "names\n(directory entries)" as Names #E2EFDA
  component "file data" as Data #E2EFDA
}

rectangle "Disk: what a power cut keeps" as Disk #FCE4D6 {
  component "durable names" as DNames #FCE4D6
  component "durable data" as DData #FCE4D6
}

queue "pending directory operations\n(create, link, rename, unlink)" as Pending #FFF2CC

App --> Names : create, link, rename, unlink\n**A1**: each is atomic, seen at once
App --> Data : write
Names --> Pending : each directory operation\nwaits here until synced
Pending --> DNames : **A2**: fsync(the directory)\nmakes its entries durable
Data --> DData : **A3**: fsync(the file)\nmakes its data durable

rectangle "Two kinds of crash" as Crashes #F8CBAD {
  card "**process crash**\n(kill, panic, abort):\nthe kernel's view survives whole" as ProcessCrash #F8CBAD
  card "**power cut**:\nthe disk's view, plus some of\nthe pending operations" as PowerCut #F8CBAD
}

Kernel ..> ProcessCrash
Disk ..> PowerCut
Pending ..> PowerCut : which survive

note bottom of PowerCut #F8CBAD
  Linux and macOS (ext4, XFS, btrfs, APFS): **any subset**
  of the pending operations survives.
  Windows (NTFS) has no directory fsync:
  **W1**: a per-volume **prefix** of the pending operations survives;
  **W2**: FlushFileBuffers on a file commits the volume's log,
  so gaze-fs syncs a file after linking or renaming it.
end note

rectangle "The same model, three times" as Models #EDEDED {
  component "gaze-fs MemFs\n(Rust tests: every crash point,\nevery surviving subset or prefix)" as MemFs #DDEBF7
  component "ProfileStartup.tla\n(TLC: every interleaving,\nup to two crashes)" as Tla #DDEBF7
  component "the real file system\n(crash-points kill tests in CI)" as Real #E2EFDA
}

Crashes ..> Models : every outcome these\ncrashes allow is checked

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#DDEBF7> | F1R3Gaze code |
  |<#E2EFDA> | operating system |
  |<#FFF2CC> | changes not yet durable |
  |<#FCE4D6> | durable state |
  |<#F8CBAD> | crashes |
  |<#EDEDED> | where the model is checked |
endlegend
@enduml
